[[Supportive care]]

Topic outline: pain management in adults with cancer.

!! Assessment
* Pain mechanism, severity, time course, and effect on function.
* Cancer-related, treatment-related, and other causes of pain.
* Urgent causes, patient goals, and barriers to pain control.

!! Nonopioid and adjuvant therapy
* Acetaminophen, NSAIDs, and neuropathic pain agents.
* Nonpharmacologic approaches and rehabilitation.

!! Opioid therapy
* Initiation, titration, and reassessment.
* Breakthrough pain and rescue dosing.
* Opioid rotation, equianalgesic conversion, and incomplete cross-tolerance.
* Renal and hepatic impairment, interactions, and safe use.

!! Adverse effects and refractory pain
* Constipation, nausea, sedation, and respiratory depression.
* Radiation, interventional procedures, and specialist referral.

